DATA PROCESSING ADDENDUM
Anthropic PBC

Effective Date: August 5, 2026
Customer: VisaCanada Inc.

This Data Processing Addendum ("DPA") forms part of the Anthropic Terms of Service and governs the processing of personal data by Anthropic on behalf of Customer.

1. DEFINITIONS
   "Personal Data" means any information relating to an identified or identifiable natural person processed by Anthropic under the Agreement.
   "Processing" has the meaning given in applicable data protection laws.

2. SCOPE AND ROLES
   Customer is the data controller. Anthropic is the data processor.
   This DPA applies to all Personal Data submitted to Claude API by Customer.

3. DATA PROTECTION OBLIGATIONS
   3.1 Anthropic will:
       - Process Personal Data only on documented instructions from Customer
       - Ensure personnel are bound by confidentiality
       - Implement appropriate technical and organizational security measures
       - Not engage sub-processors without prior written consent
       - Assist Customer with data subject rights requests
       - Delete or return Personal Data upon termination

   3.2 Security Measures:
       - Encryption in transit: TLS 1.3
       - Encryption at rest: AES-256
       - Access controls: Role-based, principle of least privilege
       - SOC 2 Type II certified infrastructure
       - Annual security audits

4. DATA RESIDENCY AND TRANSFERS
   4.1 Anthropic processes data in cloud infrastructure that meets or exceeds Canadian privacy standards (PIPEDA-equivalent protection).
   4.2 All data transfers comply with applicable data protection laws.

5. DATA RETENTION AND DELETION
   5.1 Ephemeral Processing: API requests and responses are not retained after processing is complete.
   5.2 No Training: Customer data is never used to train or improve Anthropic models.
   5.3 Immediate Deletion: All Personal Data is deleted immediately after API response delivery (< 1 second retention).

6. SECURITY BREACH NOTIFICATION
   Anthropic will notify Customer without undue delay and in any event within 72 hours of becoming aware of a personal data breach.

7. AUDIT RIGHTS
   Customer may audit Anthropic's compliance with this DPA annually upon 30 days written notice.

8. LIABILITY
   Each party's liability under this DPA is subject to the limitations in the main Agreement.

9. TERM AND TERMINATION
   This DPA remains in effect as long as Anthropic processes Personal Data on Customer's behalf.

AGREED AND ACCEPTED:

